1fs|v|To act upon; to produce an effect or change upon. ; To influence or move, as the feelings or passions; to touch. ; To love; to regard with affection. ; To show a fondness for; to like to use or practice; to choose; hence, to frequent habitually. ; To dispose or incline. ; To aim at; to aspire; to covet. ; To tend to by affinity or disposition. ; To make a show of; to put on a pretense of; to feign; to assume; as, to affect ignorance. ; To assign; to appoint.	o:124,43,7;1lmq,9,6~124,43,7;1lmq,9,6	d:2cj,13,5~2cj,13,5
